A||N||1||yobtah||'87 V6 voltage levels...||||1||
Z||000000||yobtah||08-22-2000||10:26 AM||||I have an '87 SE V6 with 73,000 miles.  Lately, I've noticed that the volt gauge shows approx. 16 volts after I've started the car cold.  As the car warms, the voltage drops until it reads between 13 and 14.  The drop usually happens over a 15 to 20 minute period of driving.  Should I be concerned about the high voltage?  If so, what might be causing it?  Thanks for any information.||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||08-22-2000||01:22 PM||||put a volt meter directly across the battery and watch what it does. If that meter is above 16 volts have the charging system checked ASAP. ((Remove and Clean the battery terminals before testing. That alone can throw things off.))<P>A fully charged battery is about 13.5 volts. Most cars will run between that and 15.5 volts when running.||||reg||1
